    Says "'Dear God, the bread,' says {innkeeper_d}, with a catch of laughter. 'You were not there at the Station? The bailiff walked the first mile. In his boots, it is true. But he walked it, and the clerk read the leave out in the round hand, and the old priest came out and said the response in a voice I have not heard from him since I was a boy. They have kept the Walk every year since, on the first of the thaw. There are forty people in my yard and not one of them has asked for credit.'".
  }
  Topic inn_after_suppressed_a with innkeeper_a "Ask {innkeeper_a} how the Walk ended" when ending(e_suppressed) once {
    Says "'They broke it up,' says {innkeeper_a}, with no expression at all. 'The Bench and the sergeant's men. Not with swords, much. With the flat, and the horses. A lot of them ran and a lot of them were taken, and you will have seen the green.' A very long wipe of the bar. 'It is quiet. I said I wanted it quiet. Nobody tell me I said it.'".
  }
  Topic inn_after_suppressed_b with innkeeper_b "Ask {innkeeper_b} how the Walk ended" when ending(e_suppressed) once {
    Says "'They broke it up,' says {innkeeper_b}, with no expression at all. 'The Bench and the sergeant's men. Not with swords, much. With the flat, and the horses. A lot of them ran and a lot of them were taken, and you will have seen the green.' A very long wipe of the bar. 'It is quiet. I said I wanted it quiet. Nobody tell me I said it.'".
  }
  Topic inn_after_suppressed_c with innkeeper_c "Ask {innkeeper_c} how the Walk ended" when ending(e_suppressed) once {
    Says "'They broke it up,' says {innkeeper_c}, with no expression at all. 'The Bench and the sergeant's men. Not with swords, much. With the flat, and the horses. A lot of them ran and a lot of them were taken, and you will have seen the green.' A very long wipe of the bar. 'It is quiet. I said I wanted it quiet. Nobody tell me I said it.'".
  }
  Topic inn_after_suppressed_d with innkeeper_d "Ask {innkeeper_d} how the Walk ended" when ending(e_suppressed) once {
    Says "'They broke it up,' says {innkeeper_d}, with no expression at all. 'The Bench and the sergeant's men. Not with swords, much. With the flat, and the horses. A lot of them ran and a lot of them were taken, and you will have seen the green.' A very long wipe of the bar. 'It is quiet. I said I wanted it quiet. Nobody tell me I said it.'".
  }
  Topic inn_after_schism_a with innkeeper_a "Ask {innkeeper_a} how the Walk ended" when ending(e_schism) once {
    Says "'There are two of them now,' says {innkeeper_a}. 'The ones who want the leave, and went home, and the Brethren, who held the Station and will not give it up. It is the old story. Both of them say they are the Walk.' A sigh. 'There is a chain on the shrine door and a stave at the Station gate. And on every milestone from here to the border there is a wheel and a cross, side by side, and every night someone rubs out the one, and every morning someone puts it back.'".
  }
  Topic inn_after_schism_b with innkeeper_b "Ask {innkeeper_b} how the Walk ended" when ending(e_schism) once {
    Says "'There are two of them now,' says {innkeeper_b}. 'The ones who want the leave, and went home, and the Brethren, who held the Station and will not give it up. It is the old story. Both of them say they are the Walk.' A sigh. 'There is a chain on the shrine door and a stave at the Station gate. And on every milestone from here to the border there is a wheel and a cross, side by side, and every night someone rubs out the one, and every morning someone puts it back.'".
  }
