    Says "'There are two of them now,' says {innkeeper_c}. 'The ones who want the leave, and went home, and the Brethren, who held the Station and will not give it up. It is the old story. Both of them say they are the Walk.' A sigh. 'There is a chain on the shrine door and a stave at the Station gate. And on every milestone from here to the border there is a wheel and a cross, side by side, and every night someone rubs out the one, and every morning someone puts it back.'".
