    Says "'There are two of them now,' says {innkeeper_d}. 'The ones who want the leave, and went home, and the Brethren, who held the Station and will not give it up. It is the old story. Both of them say they are the Walk.' A sigh. 'There is a chain on the shrine door and a stave at the Station gate. And on every milestone from here to the border there is a wheel and a cross, side by side, and every night someone rubs out the one, and every morning someone puts it back.'".
  }
  Topic inn_after_usurped_a with innkeeper_a "Ask {innkeeper_a} how the Walk ended" when ending(e_usurped) once {
    Says "'There is a new man in the bailiff's chair,' says {innkeeper_a}, 'and it is the steward. He has kept the Walk. He has put a penny on it. A stone-penny, he says, which is for the road's keeping. It is a great deal for a poor walker and not very much for a rich one, and he says that is what a toll is.' A look. 'I find I have heard that argument before. From a woman with a lead seal.'".
  }
  Topic inn_after_usurped_b with innkeeper_b "Ask {innkeeper_b} how the Walk ended" when ending(e_usurped) once {
    Says "'There is a new man in the bailiff's chair,' says {innkeeper_b}, 'and it is the steward. He has kept the Walk. He has put a penny on it. A stone-penny, he says, which is for the road's keeping. It is a great deal for a poor walker and not very much for a rich one, and he says that is what a toll is.' A look. 'I find I have heard that argument before. From a woman with a lead seal.'".
  }
